@* Rendered-markdown prose inside a ghost bubble: the `typeset typeset-chat` wrapper styles the
   classless HTML (paragraphs, list, inline code, a code block) at the bubble's own type scale -
   --typeset-size is 1em, so the prose follows the bubble instead of fighting it. *@
<div class="flex w-full max-w-md flex-col gap-5">
    <BzMessage Align="MessageAlign.End">
        <BzMessageContent>
            <BzBubble>
                <BzBubbleContent>How do I pin an item version?</BzBubbleContent>
            </BzBubble>
        </BzMessageContent>
    </BzMessage>
    <BzMessage>
        <BzMessageAvatar Class="bg-primary/10">
            <BzIcon Icon="@Icons.Outline.Sparkles" Class="text-primary size-4" />
        </BzMessageAvatar>
        <BzMessageContent>
            <BzBubble Variant="BubbleVariant.Ghost">
                <BzBubbleContent>
                    <div class="typeset typeset-chat">
                        <p>Append the version to the item name - the pin is recorded in <code>blaizio.json</code> and respected everywhere:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><code>add button@1.2.0</code> installs exactly that version.</li>
                            <li><code>update</code> re-requests a pinned item at its pin.</li>
                            <li>A later plain <code>add button</code> removes the pin.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <pre><code>blaizio add button@1.2.0</code></pre>
                        <p>Dependencies respect pins too: nothing resolves past a version you chose.</p>
                    </div>
                </BzBubbleContent>
            </BzBubble>
        </BzMessageContent>
    </BzMessage>
</div>
